# Worklog

`WORKLOG.md` is the project record of work and findings. It is append-only.

After a session changes the project, answers a question by investigating the repo, or reaches a realization about how the project behaves, append one entry at the end of `WORKLOG.md` before the session ends. If that work is committed, include the new entry in the same commit.

Each entry:

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — Short title

**Did:** What was done.

**Realized:** What turned out to be true. Omit this heading when nothing new was learned.
```

Add entries only after the last line. Leave earlier entries, and the header above the first entry, as they are.
